a verdict announced in the derrick  chauvin murder trial we're continuing  our coverage for you right now i'm  christian casadas and i'm kirsten joyce  we are checking in with the itunes  vanessa murphy  she spoke with one of nevada's most  well-known criminal defense attorneys  about the verdict  the charges and much more she joins us  live in studio  thank you for joining us vanessa well it  is rare for a jury to convict a police  officer  in america criminal defense attorney  david chesnov points to a strategy  used by the prosecution here to tell the  jury this wasn't  prosecution against police it was  prosecution against a man who happened  to be a police officer again usually  jurors  are sympathetic to law enforcement but  this jury came back with a verdict of  guilty on all three counts  chesnov says he believes both the  prosecution  and defense did a good job in this case  and he tells me he believes there's not  much  derek chovin's defense attorney could do  especially because of the video of  chauvin kneeling on george floyd's neck  i mean i i've thought of different  defenses maybe  some maybe some kind of a mental illness  defense because  to have somebody standing there in the  face of people  telling him that the person is dying and  not to do anything it's just  there was something either very sadistic  about this guy  i mean it was like a lynching  jurors deliberated for about 10 hours  before delivering the verdict
 

